    "limitations": [
      "One repetition per setting; not a confidence interval or a universal server capacity.",
      "Detailed stage probes and Python CPU sampling introduce overhead. Capacity control uses the unchanged API image without instrumentation.",
      "ACK wait includes client transport and local event-loop scheduling; not isolated RabbitMQ processing time.",
      "CPU counter intervals include preparation/initialization and HTTP drain, and exclude passive command drain.",
      "Throughput is accepted requests divided by the 15 s offered-load window; responses can finish during HTTP drain.",
      "Terminal timestamps are generated before PostgreSQL commit. Cross-clock execution timelines are approximate."
    ],
    "findings": [
      "Increasing the publisher window from 64 to 256 moves waiting from the semaphore to channel-lock acquisition; it does not eliminate the admission bottleneck.",
      "The API process consumes close to its single available core. Delay is predominantly before the AMQP confirm wait.",
      "The channel lock is held briefly; long acquisition times are not proof that the lock itself consumes most CPU.",
      "CPU samples distribute cost across HTTP handling, publisher code, AMQP background tasks and event-loop scheduling.",
      "RabbitMQ confirmation wait and resource usage show no evidence that broker admission is the dominant limit in these runs.",
      "The worker independently consumes its own CPU budget and processes fewer commands per second than are accepted, so execution queues grow."
    ]
  },
  "timing_limitations": [
    "completed_at is generated before PostgreSQL COMMIT. It does not record exact committed completion.",
    "created_at in event mode is generated by the worker and excludes broker queue wait and earlier pool wait.",
    "Counts at the submission cutoff are reconstructed from the final snapshot, not polled queue length.",
    "Client/DB UTC clock offset was not calibrated. Cross-clock cutoff and tail estimates inherit this uncertainty.",
    "Three-CPU events still had 3671 accepted commands unresolved at the stop. Time to finish all accepted work is censored; 30.360 s is only the last observed terminal timestamp.",
    "One short repetition per setting does not estimate a confidence interval or long-term sustainable capacity."
  ]
